# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks files out with CRLF, which is harmless
# for code but not for SQL: a migration that matches a multi-line string literal
# against stored text is comparing bytes, and a literal carrying \r\n silently
# matches nothing. That is exactly how 20260831120000_secciones_y_recusacion.sql
# came to abort — the recusación block never matched, the section numeral
# survived, and the migration rolled back with a message that pointed at the
# template rather than at the line endings.
#
# Migrations are the load-bearing case, so they are pinned explicitly; the rest
# of the tree is normalised too, so a diff never turns into a whole-file rewrite.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sql text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
